## Eastman Color Negative 5251: Beeler, Morris and Simonds (Eastman Kodak), "A New, Higher Speed Color Negative Film", J. SMPTE 77 (Sept 1968), 988-990, on Type 5254, which it states is identical to Type 5251 in structure, spectral sensitivity and dyes, one stop faster. Its 300 dpi scanned figures traced by dev/film/trace_raster_curves.py: Fig. 1 spectral sensitivity (relative S, log); Fig. 2 dye absorption (densities as drawn, with the neutral); Fig. 3 printing densities onto Eastman Color Print 5385, process ECN (SD-30, 12 min at 21 C). Fig. 3's log exposure axis is unlabelled: its two ticks are taken as 1.0 log H apart and its origin set so that green is 0.80 over D-min at log H -0.70 (an estimate, see grey_log_h).. D-min and MTF: EXR 200T 5293's; granularity: rms 13, an estimate.
